{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1541106-author-kith","id":1541106,"title":"Author Kith","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-08-27T20:18:08-07:00","id":1541106,"title":"Author Kith","content":"Here's an idea for an Author Kith. Comment on how useful it is please, or how it could be best changed. Thanks!<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:28px\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><span style=\"font-family:Vivaldi\"><span style=\"color:#76923c\">Author</span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"color:#76923c\"><i> Unless you enjoy drooling and screaming, I wouldn\u2019t read that particular scroll if I were you.</i></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><span style=\"font-family:Times\"> Stolen by Keepers even more egotistical than usual, authors were forced to invent intricate and original tales, meticulously diary everything their master did and said, or to spread their master\u2019s legend in poetic form. In any case, the author eventually learns how to use the magic of Faerie to pen words into a semblance of reality and use that power to write themselves an escape. Back home, Authors can still use the written word as a way of enforcing their will on the world and are either treasured or feared by the Courts for their ability to do so.<br /> <br /> <i> Beast:</i> The city hosts a circle of beastly authors: one resembles a raven, one an owl, and another a lizard. They all have a predilection for glasses, ruffs and waistcoats.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><i><span style=\"font-family:Times\"> Darkling:</span></i><span style=\"font-family:Times\"> She looks at you like she\u2019s reading the end of a book, and her fingers leave ink stains everywhere.<br /> <br /> <i> Elemental:</i> His fingers glow with power, and he traces directly into the air like a sparkler; full sentences puffing away into smoke.<br /> <br /> <i> Fairest:</i> She's interested in <i>you;</i> you're <i>her</i> muse. She turns your life into perfect iambic pentameter on the spot and slams poetry that describe your every secret thought.<br /> <br /> <i> Grimm:</i> Like a visitor straight from the eighteenth century, scruffy from travel, and on the bones of his arse. But that book he carries everywhere is wrought in gold.<br /> <br /> <i> Ogre:</i> She's tall, articulate and elegant, but, damn, the way she holds that pen makes you <i>very</i> nervous.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><i><span style=\"font-family:Times\"> Wizened:</span></i><span style=\"font-family:Times\"> He distractedly chews paper that seems to constantly \u201cleak\u201d from his badly patched clothes.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Times\"> Kith Blessing:</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Times\"> When an Author rolls Expression to do with wordy endeavours, three successes count as an exceptional success.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><span style=\"font-family:Times\"><i> Dark</i> <i>Materials:</i> An Author can hide a secret message in any writing at least a paragraph long with the expenditure of a point of Glamour and an Intelligence + Expression + Wyrd roll. This message can only be read by as many people as the Author has dots of Clarity, less if they wish. For another point of Glamour, anyone else not privy to the secret, and who reads the text, must roll higher than the Author\u2019s successes with Resolve + Investigation + Wyrd, or be struck with one of the following Conditions: Amnesia, Delusional, Disoriented, Dissociation, Frightened or Madness. The text retains this power for a week per point of the 